+## Switch packed EE boundary correction (M02, 2026-11-08)
+
+[gta-recomp] Maintained root overlay `0002-packed-architectural-semantics.patch`
+fixes architectural lane selection in PINTH, PINTEH, PEXEH, PEXEW and PROT3W.
+PSLLVW/PSRLVW/PSRAVW use rs counts and rt even data words, with independent
+sign extension to each 64-bit destination. Generic four-word intrinsic helpers
+remain separate. The PEXEH/PROT3W generator paths now call the verified macros
+instead of duplicating stale inline shuffles. Existing generator rs/rt order
+is preserved. Numeric and architectural tests belong to the root port.
+
+Reference inspected: PCSX2 MMI interpreter at
+https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2/blob/4223d03c58f8fd1787da7af28fe80c2140e1a22a/pcsx2/MMI.cpp
+(PSLLVW/PSRLVW, PINTH, PEXEH/PEXEW/PROT3W, PSRAVW, PINTEH). The new code
+is a scalar/portable implementation of those documented operation contracts,
+not an imported emulator source file. No game-generated source is included.
+
+The pinned user-game generation has no calls to these named helpers; the tests
+therefore exercise synthetic operands explicitly. Compilation/native results
+do not establish target execution; the consolidated Switch run remains required.
